.DS_Store
*.zip
node_modules/
.env
package.json
package-lock.json
.claude/
test-results/
playwright-report/
settings.local.json
tests/flow/.local-accounts.json

# EVERY local screenshot, by WHERE it lands rather than what it is called.
#
# This was eleven per-family patterns, and the comment on the last batch said
# out loud that a rule per family means the next family added is not covered
# "without anyone remembering this file exists". One commit later a throwaway
# jack-*.png probe proved it, which is the second time the same list has been
# extended after the fact.
#
# The screenshot specs all write to the repo ROOT (the path they pass is
# relative to cwd), and every real image asset in this repo lives in a
# subdirectory: icons/icon-180, -192, -512 are the only tracked PNGs. So the
# root anchor is the whole rule, it needs no maintenance, and icons/ and any
# future subdirectory asset are untouched by construction.
/*.png

# native/ is a real npm package the iOS build needs; the blanket package.json
# ignore above predates it and silently dropped it from the first workflow PR.
#
# The wildcard is deliberate. This used to be one line per plugin, and build 19
# proved why that is a trap: six new plugins were added, nobody remembered to
# add six more lines, and their package.json files were silently never
# committed. Capacitor then found 6 plugins instead of 12 and the build shipped
# without them. One pattern covers every plugin ever added.
!native/package.json
!native/*/package.json
tests/flow/.local-crew.json
tests/flow/.local-showcase.json
tests/flow/.local-showcase-messy.json
local-visual-shots/

# Python bytecode. py_compile drops these next to any script it checks, and
# they got committed once already by a git add -A.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
